    11	# Pod v3 environment runs flash-attn 2.8.3 forward on sm_120
    12	
    13	Phase 6.0 of the rebuild set up a **separate v3 environment** on pod `w7ia3zvxqsvs3g`, and the model's forced packed FlashAttention path **runs forward on sm_120**. This clears the "no flash-attn on the pod" blocker for the forward path only. Trunk numerics, backward, rollout, PPO and evaluation are not qualified here.
    14	
    15	## Environment
    16	
    17	- Checkout: `/workspace/kg-v3-rebuild`, from `kg/isaiah-gap-closure` @ `69397da` via a git bundle, detached and clean (post-run receipt).
    18	- Venv: `/workspace/kg-v3-rebuild/.venv`, built with `uv sync --frozen --group dev --extra flash-attn`.
    19	- Installed: torch 2.9.0+cu128, triton 3.5.0, flash-attn 2.8.3 (`pod/versions.json`).
    20	- flash-attn came from a **prebuilt release wheel**, `flash_attn-2.8.3+cu12torch2.9cxx11abiTRUE-cp312-cp312-linux_x86_64.whl`, which the lock's sdist downloads with `FLASH_ATTENTION_SKIP_CUDA_BUILD=TRUE`. No compile ran. The installed `.so` holds 72 sm_120 cubins alongside sm_80/90/100 (`cuobjdump --list-elf`).
    21	- The Rust extension is a **dev-profile** (unoptimized) `maturin develop` build. Build `--release` before any environment-throughput measurement.
    22	
    23	## What ran
    24	
    25	- **Kernel against SDPA.** `flash_attn_varlen_func` on BF16 packed q/k/v (8 heads × 32, 256 sequences, 173,518 tokens) matches an fp32 per-sequence SDPA reference as closely as BF16 SDPA does (max |Δ| 0.00359 for both). Flash and BF16 SDPA differ by at most 2⁻⁸, within BF16 spacing at the observed magnitudes. No element falls outside `0.02 + 0.02|ref|`.
    26	- **Model trunk.** With the preset `configs/model/kaggriculture.yaml` (`force_flash_attn: true`) under bf16 autocast, the packed flash path ran in both the **eager** and the **compiled** (`max-autotune-no-cudagraphs`, dynamic) trunk forward. The profiler records `flash::flash_fwd_kernel` in both, with one `pack_sequence` call per forward.
    27	- **Tests on the pod.** `tests/owl/model/test_attn.py` passed 7 of 7, including the flash-backend test that skips on the Mac; `tests/kaggriculture` passed 161 of 161.
    28	
    29	## Limits
    30	
    31	- **Forward only.** The flash backward kernels and compiled backward through the packed trunk were not exercised. At `69397da` the heads did not exist and the model was not wired into `run_ppo`.
    32	- **Trunk numerics are not qualified.** In every trunk comparison (compiled vs eager flash, flash vs padded SDPA), 0.017–0.021 % of present-token elements fall outside `0.02 + 0.02|ref|`, with max |Δ| up to 0.087. BF16 rounding over 8 layers is a plausible explanation, not a proven one. The discriminating check, an fp32 reference with autocast and TF32 off that retains outlier magnitudes and locations, has not run.
    33	- The timings in the smoke are single profiled forwards, not throughput evidence.
    34	
    35	## Hazards
    36	
    37	- **Wheel custody.** The torch 2.9 wheel is a release asset added on 2025-12-17, after the v2.8.3 tag. `setup.py` resolves it by URL, and `uv.lock` pins only the sdist hash. A rebuilt pod could therefore resolve a different kernel **without any lock change**. Recheck both digests after any rebuild:
    38	  - wheel sha256 `4e2f9e39313266b1544b68138b15b91ee6221eccf14f7902b7c6620351340810` (equals the GitHub release digest at install time);
    39	  - installed `flash_attn_2_cuda` `.so` sha256 `8ca052bf2d3f53baa629e22749b9622a95273c5bffb5f06cd24768ef63f65807`, byte-identical to the wheel member (`cmp` exit 0).
    40	- **Hard-linked venvs.** 19,796 files in `/workspace/kg-v3/.venv` share inodes with the new venv through the uv cache. An in-place edit of a file in either venv changes the other. Avoid in-place edits of installed files, or create venvs with `uv --link-mode=copy`.
    41	- **Operator-reported custody.** "No credentials copied" and "nothing pushed" have no retained receipt. The only evidence is the clone's remote list, which shows just the bundle path.
    42	
    43	## Consequences
    44	
    45	- Phases 6.1–6.4 use this venv or reproduce both digests above. Any pod rebuild verifies the release-asset digest before trusting the kernel.
    46	- 6.1 must still cover flash backward, rollout, the PPO update and evaluation, and should run the fp32 discriminating trunk check.
    47	- Earlier "no flash-attn on the pod" statements, including the FlashAttention limit in the [[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiled-GEMM Reference]], predate this setup. That note's revision belongs to the ATEN implementation lane.
    48	
    49	## Verification
    50	
    51	- Codex reviewed the receipts twice: `verify-flash-attn-r1` (APPROVE WITH EDITS, edits applied in `78df33c`) and `verify-flash-attn-r2` (APPROVE). The reports are local working transcripts in `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/codex/`, not committed.
    52	- On this checkout, `shasum -a 256 -c MANIFEST.sha256` in `flash-attn-setup-2026-09-29/pod/` reports 30 of 30 files OK (2026-09-29). This checks local custody of the receipts, not the pod's live venv.
    53	- The wheel-member receipt (`pod/wheel_member_compare.txt`) and the cubin listing are the retained evidence for the digest and sm_120 claims.
    54	
    55	Concept search before writing: the [[compiled-gemm-template-overflows-above-2-21-rows|compiled-GEMM Reference]] (FlashAttention limit), the [[../decisions/restart-the-port-from-isaiahs-clean-base|restart Decision]] (flash-attn pin unchanged), the historical [[shared-ppo-adapts-game-batches-without-a-second-loop|shared-PPO Reference]] (reference-branch FlashAttention use) and the [[../decisions/start-multi-gpu-qualification-with-two-ranks|multi-GPU Decision]] (host facts live in ops). None records a current-tree flash-attn environment. The [[kaggriculture-encoder-reuses-isaiah-stateless-layers|encoder Reference]] leaves CUDA flash execution to Phase 6; this note is that first, forward-only step. Full evidence: `ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/results.md`, "Phase 6.0 — flash-attn on the pod".
